  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Guardian Foundation, incubator for independent media</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Guardian Foundation, inkubator f&#xf6;r oberoende media</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">The Guardian Foundation har ans&#xf6;kt till Sida om finansiering p&#xe5;  9 781 200  SEK f&#xf6;r att genomf&#xf6;ra insatsen &quot;Incubator for Independent Turkish Media&quot; under &#xe5;ren 2020-2023.

Insatsen syftar till att bygga kapacitet och st&#xf6;dja h&#xf6;gkvalitativa oberoende turkiska medier f&#xf6;r att bidra till en stark och r&#xe4;ttvis demokrati d&#xe4;r medierna har kraft att p&#xe5;verka och agera och det civila samh&#xe4;llet har kunskap och k&#xe4;nner sig bemyndigad att agera. 

Insatsens totala finansiering &#xe4;r 9 781 200 SEK och Sida &#xe4;r ensam finansi&#xe4;r. Runt 6,46 miljoner SEK av insatsens budget kommer att vidaref&#xf6;rmedlas fr&#xe5;n Guardian Foundation till organisationen  Dijital Medya Arastirmalari Dernegi  (DMRA) i Turkiet.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Guardian Foundation has applied to Sida for funding of SEK 9 781 200  to implement the initiative &quot;Incubator for Independent Turkish Media&quot; during the years 2020-2023.

The effort aims to build capacity and support high-quality independent Turkish media to contribute to a strong and fair democracy where the media have the power to influence and act and civil society has the knowledge and authority to act.

The total financing of the initiative is SEK 9 781 200 and Sida is the sole financier. Around SEK 6.46 million of the initiative&apos;s budget will be passed on from the Guardian Foundation to the organization Dijital Medya Arastirmalari Dernegi(DMRA)  based in Turkey</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The intervention is based on the premise that a functioning independent media landscape contributes to better informed citizens who are able to participate meaningfully in democratic processs. The objective of the intervention is to build capacity of and support high quality independent Turkish journalism so that it contributes to a strong and just democracy where civil society are informed and empowered to participate, influence and act.&#xa0;It also aims to support the development of a range of new media concepts such as podcasts, online magazines and YouTube channels.</narrative>
  </description>
